From 1a6935d2e7b008c4e84373d52cc826845e2c1cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:14:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix show_logo template path; document that it is unused

show_logo pointed at shots/GLOBALS/logo/teardrop.png -- a folder that does
not exist. The _globals convention is already used by the LUT paths a few
lines above in this file; show_logo was missed when that move happened.

Corrected to shots/_globals/logo/teardrop_blk1.png, which is the file the
bake actually uses, and annotated with two things that were not obvious:

1. NOTHING in FlowTrackingConfig resolves this template. Verified by grep.
   The slate logo is hardcoded in qt_bake_oiio.py (BUF_Mac_watcher) as
   LOGO_PATH. Editing this template does not change the slate -- that has
   to happen in the other repo. The template is corrected so it stops
   being actively misleading, not because it does anything.

2. qt_bake_oiio.py guards the logo with os.path.exists() and silently
   renders an unbranded slate when it is missing. A wrong logo path is a
   silent quality regression, not a visible failure -- worth knowing given
   the 2026-08-17 incident where a silent watcher failure went unnoticed
   for over a week.

Confirmed on disk 2026-08-19: the folder holds teardrop.png,
teardrop_blk.png and teardrop_blk1.png. teardrop_blk and teardrop_blk1 are
the same size (likely duplicates). Only teardrop_blk1.png is world-readable
(rw-r--r--); the other two are rw-------, which would break the bake if the
watcher ever ran as a different user.
---
 core/templates.yml | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/templates.yml b/core/templates.yml
index be246f2..a010d4a 100644
--- a/core/templates.yml
+++ b/core/templates.yml
@@ -528,7 +528,21 @@ paths:
         definition: 'editorial/to_editorial/{YYYY}_{MM}_{DD}/{Shot}_{Step}[_{nuke.output}]_v{version}.mov'
 
     show_logo:
-        definition: 'shots/GLOBALS/logo/teardrop.png'
+        # UNUSED BY THIS CONFIG as of 2026-08-19 -- nothing in FlowTrackingConfig
+        # resolves this template. Kept in sync with reality so it isn't
+        # misleading, but EDITING IT DOES NOT CHANGE THE SLATE.
+        #
+        # The slate logo is hardcoded in qt_bake_oiio.py (BUF_Mac_watcher) as
+        # LOGO_PATH = .../shots/_globals/logo/teardrop_blk1.png -- change it
+        # THERE. Note that script guards with os.path.exists() and silently
+        # renders an unbranded slate if the file is missing, so a bad path
+        # here fails quietly rather than loudly.
+        #
+        # Was 'shots/GLOBALS/logo/teardrop.png' -- that folder does not exist;
+        # the _globals convention (see LUT paths above) is correct.
+        # Folder contains teardrop.png, teardrop_blk.png, teardrop_blk1.png;
+        # only _blk1 is world-readable and only _blk1 is the one in use.
+        definition: 'shots/_globals/logo/teardrop_blk1.png'
 
     ep_nuke_shot_render_flag:
         definition: '@shot_base/render/work/{Shot}_{Step}[_{nuke.output}]_v{version}/.render_complete_{Shot}_{Step}[_{nuke.output}]_v{version}.json'
-- 
